<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trincomalee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trincomalee is a port city on the north-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> with one of the largest natural deep-water harbours in the world. It is the site of the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> Koneswaram temple. Its harbour was contested by the Portuguese, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, French and British, and it served as an important British naval base until 1957.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trincomalee.jpg" alt="Trincomalee" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kondephy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bay_of_Trincomalee.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
